# E6 Connect is disabled by default. Copying this file does not enable it.
# LAN and Tailscale pairing work without these values. Uncomment all four
# public values together to build against the development Clerk instance.
# The publishable key and client id are public. Do not add server-side secrets
# to this file.
#
# This pk_test key is the development instance
# (renewing-iguana-1351.clerk.accounts.dev). Production builds need a pk_live key
# from a production Clerk instance whose Frontend API is clerk.e6code.com.

# Development Clerk instance. To use your own, get these from the Clerk Dashboard
# under API keys, JWT templates, and OAuth applications.
# E6CODE_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_cmVuZXdpbmctaWd1YW5hLTEzNTEuY2xlcmsuYWNjb3VudHMuZGV2JA
# E6CODE_CLERK_JWT_TEMPLATE=e6-relay
# E6CODE_CLERK_CLI_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=h6ESQYyHMe9JQ6uZ

# Optional: signed macOS passkey builds. The RP domain defaults to the Frontend API
# hostname encoded in E6CODE_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY. Set the override only when Clerk
# returns a different RP ID or when multiple domains must be entitled.
# E6CODE_APPLE_TEAM_ID=ABC1234567
# E6CODE_MACOS_PROVISIONING_PROFILE=/absolute/path/to/e6code.provisionprofile
# E6CODE_CLERK_PASSKEY_RP_DOMAINS=example.clerk.accounts.dev,clerk.example.com

# Production relay. For a self-hosted relay, `infra/relay` deploys update it
# automatically. Uncomment with the three Clerk values above.
# E6CODE_RELAY_URL=https://relay.e6code.com

# Optional: hosted app origin used by the CLI's out-of-band OAuth flow.
# Defaults to https://latest.app.e6code.com; override to test against nightly.
# E6CODE_HOSTED_APP_URL=https://nightly.app.e6code.com

# Public, ingest-only mobile OpenTelemetry configuration.
# E6CODE_MOBILE_OTLP_TRACES_URL=https://api.axiom.co/v1/traces
# E6CODE_MOBILE_OTLP_TRACES_DATASET=e6-code-mobile-traces-dev
# E6CODE_MOBILE_OTLP_TRACES_TOKEN=xaat-...
